*** Add File:services/excel/README_EXCEL_INTEGRATION.md
+# Aegis Excel Integration - Overview
+
+This patch adds:
+- Backend proxy (services/excel/backend_proxy.py) — validates OIDC tokens and proxies requests to internal Aegis services.
+- Office Add-in scaffold (taskpane.html + taskpane.js + manifest.xml) — minimal evidence-backed Q&A UI with "Insert answer" and "Request Review".
+- Power Query snippet (services/excel/powerquery/PowerQuerySnippet.txt) to fetch reports into Excel.
+- Kubernetes manifests to deploy the backend proxy and host the Add-in static assets.
+
+Security & deployment notes:
+- Register an Azure AD app for the Add-in and set CLIENT_ID + OIDC_ISSUER in the proxy deployment.
+- Do NOT embed SERVICE_API_KEY in client code. The Add-in must obtain a user token via MSAL and call the backend proxy; backend uses SERVICE_API_KEY to call internal Aegis services.
+- For production host Add-in static content on HTTPS (cdn or ingress) and set SourceLocation in manifest to that URL.
+- Wire human_queue URL and Aegis internal endpoints via cluster DNS or service mesh.
+
+Quick deploy (operator):
+1. Build and push proxy image (from services/excel/backend_proxy.py).
+2. Create Kubernetes secrets: aegis-secrets (azure_client_id, service_api_key).
+3. Apply configmap (or host static add-in files in CDN) and deployments:
+   kubectl apply -f services/excel/k8s/addin-configmap.yaml
+   kubectl apply -f services/excel/k8s/addin-static-deployment.yaml
+   kubectl apply -f services/excel/k8s/backend-deployment.yaml
+4. Update manifest.xml SourceLocation to https://<addin-host>/taskpane.html and sideload or publish add-in via Office 365 admin center.
+
